{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "RecurrenceSliceBatch",
    "description": "THE SLICE PIN (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.19.2, esm-spec 4.3.1.1 point 4). V[j,k] = c[j] at k = 1 and a[j]*V[j,k-1] + b[j] after it, over 64 independent cells j and 6 positions k along the recurrence axis k. The cells that share one k form a SLICE; no cell reads another cell of its own slice, so a binding MAY evaluate a slice's 64 cells together (vectorized or kernel-merged), but only with each cell's operations unchanged. a, b and c are chosen so that a fused multiply-add changes the last bit at 128 of the 384 cells: V[1,6] is -2.69615290308142 by the sequential sweep; evaluating a[j]*V[j,k-1] + b[j] as one fused multiply-add at every step gives -2.6961529030814204 instead. Zero tolerance: a batched path that contracts the multiply and the add into an FMA, or that evaluates a slice before the previous one is complete, fails here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "recurrence",
      "slice",
      "batching",
      "fma",
      "bit-identical"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "cells": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 64
    },
    "steps": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 6
    }
  },
